 "arc": "Two-step: a lateral travelling step with the weight swinging between the feet on a steady four-count. Frames 0-3 carry the weight over the character-left foot and reach across with the arms opening wide to the sides; the character-right foot is on the ball, ready to release. Frames 4-7 are the weight change — the arms drop and swing low past the hips as anticipation, then the character-right leg crosses behind and the body settles onto it with a slight lean to character-right.\n\nFrames 8-11 are the recovery: arms lift back up and out, the character-right foot unweights and the hips counter-rotate character-right against the shoulders. Frames 12-15 settle the weight back to centre on the balls of both feet, arms back to waist height, so the last frame arrives on both feet in the same open stance frame 0 starts from. The seam is a single step across the cut — keep the arm swing continuous through it, do not re-plant.",
